<!--Post: 643--><!--Time: 1091074822-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST643"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, July 28, 2004 - 9:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Since the police have been so mute about the details of the crime scenes, the papers have so far stated that only Joey Otero was hooded. Since BTK&#39;s targets are female, there was something about killing that little boy that hit close to BTK&#39;s home. He covered the boy&#39;s face to depersonalize him. Perhaps Joey was around BTK&#39;s age when his father left him with a mother/mother figure that depersonalized him by ridicule, emasculation, etc. She took away that which could have been so good and replaced it with Factor X: the blood lust. The compulsion that all addicts face. It may be the drive to kill, eat, binge, porn, child molestation, or any of those hidden demons that remain known only to the person keeping the secret. The masturbation at the crime scenes suggest that BTK cannot have sexual relations with living or dead persons. <BR> <BR>It is difficult to imagine that he has not killed during the time that he appeared &#39;silent&#39;. He can live off the thrill of his souvenirs, and taunting the authorities is certainly a way to sublimate his urges. He does want to get caught, as his notoriety will be unparalleled. And, as victims&#39; families can attest, those convicted live long past their convictions as they wrangle with the criminal justice system. He will live out his life, perhaps incarcerated, while he makes money and enjoys the fame of giving interviews, book rights, movie rights, and the like. <BR> <BR>Does he have photos of Joey&#39;s face? Only BTK knows. Only the public will know when he allows us that knowledge. BTK did have feelings but someone took them away. That someone should have protected and nurtured. Instead, they betrayed the vulnerable child entrusted to their safekeeping. The repercussions have been devastating. <BR> <BR>BTK is the &#39;Boy in the Box&#39; who survived. Nothing in his past can justify his actions. Only he can tell use what it is like to live in a vacuum filled with demons.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 643-->
<!--Post: 645--><!--Time: 1091091477-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST645"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 29, 2004 - 1:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with you. I believe there are more victims. <BR> <BR>You touch on a subject that I&#39;d like to comment upon. I mention &#34;Factor X&#34; here only because the actual term in your post reminded me of the concept, or whatever it&#39;s supposed to be. <BR> <BR>While mentally unbalanced, BTK has shown that he knows how plan murders, his taunts prove he knows <BR>what he&#39;s doing is viewed by society as very wrong. He knows it&#39;s first-degree murder. <BR> <BR>And that is why I don&#39;t buy &#34;Factor X&#34; for one second. &#40;I&#39;m sure you don&#39;t, either, Teardrop, as I say, your mention of the term reminded me of something I&#39;ve wanted to say for a while, and am now saying.&#41; <BR> <BR>All this crap about &#34;I can&#39;t help myself,&#34; and internal &#34;devils&#34; or whatnot, the &#34;I&#39;m driven to kill&#34; attitude. WRONG! <BR>You had a choice, BTK and you know it. I see a pretty woman walking down the street, sure I may envision a pleasant physical encounter. But I don&#39;t stalk her, I don&#39;t run across the street and rape her and I sure as heck don&#39;t torture and kill her. <BR>You&#39;re no monster. You&#39;re a weak-willed poltroon who preys upon the easiest targets. Oh, you had a tough childhood? So did I. Like millions of children I was often covered with bruises and sometimes with blood. I&#39;ve managed to remain violence-free, as have almost all abused kids. <BR> <BR>I realize there&#39;s an unspoken &#34;Don&#39;t write anything which might antagonize BTK; remember, it may only take one sympathetic, well-crafted post <BR>and he&#39;ll just walk right into the nearest police station and surrender&#34; attitude on every BTK board on the Internet. We&#39;re all grown-ups, we know this sexual sadist isn&#39;t going to fall for any of that. <BR>BTK, you have won. For now. Since you are completely bereft of a conscience, let me put this in terms you&#39;ll appreciate. You have the CONTROL, pathetic and unmanly as it is, at present. You can have CONTROL until the end of time if you want it, but you know what that requires.  <BR> <BR>Settle your affairs, use the high IQ I know you have and get a lawyer to enable you to work out a bargain with the powers that be. <BR>You can still call the shots. The time is drawing near when you&#39;ll lose the ability to control your fate and if you remain anonymous, you&#39;ll be lucky if you end up a tiny trivia question by the year 2015. <BR>The choice is yours.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 645-->
